==English==

===Etymology===
Recorded since 1297, from {{etyl|fro}} [[encountrer]] "confront," from [[encontre]] "against, counter to", from Late Latin [[incontra]] "in front of", itself from {{etyl|la}} [[in-]] "in" + [[contra]] "against"

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-encounter.ogg|Audio (US)}}
*: {{rhymes|aʊntə(r)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{transitive}} To [[meet]] (someone) or find (something) [[unexpectedly]].
# {{transitive}} To [[confront]] (someone or something), notably face to face.
# {{transitive}} To [[engage]] in [[conflict]], as with an enemy.

